# shir_nodes/foreach_line.node — STREAMING line iteration over a file.
#
# The dynamic-source primitive: reduces `cmd file` / `grep P F | cmd`
# pipelines to a lazy per-line loop — O(1) memory (O(limit) for early-exit
# heads), never slurps the file where bash itself streams. Body statements
# use the existing VALUE primitives (FieldExtract/Contains/RegSub/…) per
# line. limit=None reads to EOF; Some(expr) stops after that many lines
# (`head -n K F`) — backends close the reader early.
#
# Backends: Perl while(<$fh>)+last, JS sh2.eachLine(path,cb,limit),
# C getline, Go bufio.Scanner, Zig reader loop.

node ForEachLine
tag "ForEachLine"
field source: expr
field var: string
field body: stmts
field limit: optional_expr
# Unstated — the missing component is a STREAM AND COST MODEL: reader state and its
# position, laziness (O(1) memory, O(limit) for early-exit heads), closing the reader at
# the limit, and IO errors. The VALUE side is already available — the visited sequence is
# `lines_of` from the take_lines/reg_sub model, and its truncation at `limit` is `take` —
# but a law about it would restate those definitions rather than say anything about the
# streaming behaviour this node exists for. Recorded as a named missing model rather than
# the bare word "effect".
spec: none (unstated: missing model — stream/cost model (reader position, laziness and
# memory bound, early close at the limit, IO errors); the visited multiset is `lines_of`,
# which carries no streaming claim.)
